1
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:04,333
Part Two: Your Nutrition Support Team

2
00:00:05,541 --> 00:00:08,875
You are not alone in your treatment
and nutrition goals.

3
00:00:09,125 --> 00:00:11,708
In addition to your doctor and their team,

4
00:00:11,708 --> 00:00:14,458
from the beginning
to the end of your treatment,

5
00:00:14,458 --> 00:00:17,833
you will have the support
of our department's dedicated dietitian

6
00:00:18,166 --> 00:00:20,666
and speech Therapy team.

7
00:00:20,666 --> 00:00:24,291
Our dietitian will provide guidance
and give general advice

8
00:00:24,291 --> 00:00:27,958
about what to eat
and how to get more calories in.

9
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:31,041
Any questions you may have about nutrition

10
00:00:31,041 --> 00:00:34,041
or your diet can be addressed to them.

11
00:00:34,041 --> 00:00:38,208
Be sure to see the dietitian every week
during your treatment.

12
00:00:38,708 --> 00:00:41,375
In addition to our dedicated dietitian,

13
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,666
we have a group of speech
and language therapists.

14
00:00:44,666 --> 00:00:50,041
Their job is to make sure you are
swallowing well so you can eat and drink.

15
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:52,875
To do this, they will
have you complete a series

16
00:00:52,875 --> 00:00:56,250
of tests
and perform strengthening exercises.

17
00:00:56,833 --> 00:01:00,875
One test is the modified barium swallow study,

18
00:01:00,875 --> 00:01:04,541
which is usually done
two months after finishing radiation.

19
00:01:04,541 --> 00:01:07,500
Unless you are at a higher
risk of choking,

20
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,125
also known as aspiration.

21
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:13,333
The team will
have you drink a liquid containing a dye

22
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:18,125
that will allow them to see your 
swallowing function using X-ray imaging. 

23
00:01:18,416 --> 00:01:19,458
Specifically, 

24
00:01:19,458 --> 00:01:23,583
they are verifying that the liquid
is going down the proper pathway:

25
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:25,333
The esophagus.

26
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:29,916
 Food or liquid incorrectly entering
the airway is called aspiration

27
00:01:29,916 --> 00:01:33,125
and is something that we want to avoid.

28
00:01:33,416 --> 00:01:35,291
In addition to these tests,

29
00:01:35,291 --> 00:01:39,875
the speech therapy team will also teach
you exercises to engage

30
00:01:39,875 --> 00:01:43,958
and strengthen your chewing, swallowing,
and speaking muscles.

31
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:49,958
Much like exercising the body at the gym,
these exercises maintain good,

32
00:01:49,958 --> 00:01:55,250
healthy function of these muscles
so you can continue to eat and drink well.
